From 055e8c92408e5a1755e384a052b7140dc77c402e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frederic Petrignani <frederic.petrignani@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:21:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] quartic: report the disagreement between the two
 finite-difference routes to phi_iijj (Hessian route)

For i != j the semi-diagonal quartic constant can be formed from the Hessians
displaced along j (element ii) or along i (element jj). assemble_quartic_from_hessians
averaged the two, after which check_quartic's phi[i,j] vs phi[j,i] comparison is
trivially satisfied, so numerical noise in the input Hessians went unnoticed.

- keep both routes, average as before (numerics unchanged), and print a summary of
  |route a - route b| (median, 90th percentile, max, worst pairs) with a warning above
  10 cm-1; the statistics are stored in findifrec['quartic_route_report']
- document in check_quartic what it does and does not check
- tutorial: DISP_SIZE guidance for programs whose Hessians are themselves finite
  differences of gradients (psi4 for DFT functionals without analytic Hessians)
- tests on a synthetic quartic potential: exact Hessians give zero disagreement and
  reproduce phi_ijk and phi_iijj; 0.05 cm-1 of noise on one displaced Hessian at
  DISP_SIZE 0.05 is flagged (about 20 cm-1 in phi_iijj)

Motivation: benzene, B3LYP/6-31G*, psi4 1.10.2 Hessians (finite differences of
gradients), DISP_SIZE 0.05: the two routes disagreed by a median of 22 cm-1 and up to
1265 cm-1 while the run reported 'No inconsistencies found'.
